# Multiplayer-safe scripting

Design every gameplay system so a hosted game with clients would stay in sync. The user cannot run host+client tests until there are real focus trees. Do not ask for a live MP lobby as a gate. Take extra time on scripted effects, GUI, on_actions, and variables instead.

**Do**
- Country-scoped effects only (`on_monthly`, scripted GUI effects on ROOT)
- Deterministic math: same inputs must yield the same treasury, ideas, and stockpiles
- Shared country/global variables; identical tech costs for every tag
- Prefer file/sanity checks (`tools/check_mp_skeleton.py` or equivalent)

**Do not**
- `random`, `random_list`, or client-only / UI-only variables that change gameplay
- Patch Arms Against Tyranny International Market payment (CIC is hardcoded)
- Invent new `map/buildings.txt` spawn types
- Block work on “please test with 2 clients” until the user asks

Live host+clients OOS testing comes later, after focus trees.
